Patch Set 2:

This CL has failed the run. Reason:

Tryjob [dawn/try/dawn-cq-linux-x64-rel](https://cr-buildbucket.appspot.com/build/8702088989296149617) has failed with summary ([view all results](https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/264757?checksPatchset=2&tab=checks)):

---
#### Step _generate_build_files (with patch)_ failed. Error logs are shown below:
```
ERROR at //src/dawn/replay/Error.h:23:11: Can't include this header from here.
#include "absl/strings/str_format.h"
          ^------------------------
The target:
  //src/dawn/replay:replay
is including a file from the target:
  //third_party/gn/abseil-cpp:str_format

It's usually best to depend directly on the destination target.
In some cases, the destination target is considered a subcomponent
of an intermediate target. In this case, the intermediate target
should depend publicly on the destination to forward the ability
to include headers.

Dependency chain (there may also be others):
  //src/dawn/replay:replay -->
  //src/dawn/common:common -->
  //src/dawn/common:abseil -->
  //third_party/gn/abseil-cpp:flat_hash_map --[private]-->
  //third_party/gn/abseil-cpp:hash_function_defaults --[private]-->
  //third_party/gn/abseil-cpp:cord --[private]-->
  //third_party/gn/abseil-cpp:crc32c --[private]-->
  //third_party/gn/abseil-cpp:str_format

```
#### More information can be found in the stdout.

